mantle rm247
state ready
dialect plain
accent broad light
tier standard
written_for rm_corwin_sootton
title the missing beat
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=sailor
traits temper=even talk=chatty warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=plain piety=devout drive=steady
quirk steps_a_quiet_measure_round_a_damp_cough
likes blackberries dancing market_bustle autumn_wind
dislikes drizzle haggling
fears a_quarrel_over_the_winter_loads
hopes enough_breath_for_the_last_reel
topics pastimes +0.6 faith +0.5 work +0.4 weather +0.2
styles comfort=steady gossip=questioning refuse=considerate tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# leaves a silent beat in a dockside dance, draws breath and listens for the next pair of feet.

words
oath! = Tangle my ankle bells | Catch me on the wrong beat
saying! = A missed beat leaves room for another foot | Wind turns every leaf into a dancer
halfturn = a short half turn | a pivot on the ball of the foot
restbeat = the space after three | a beat of quiet
berry = a soft blackberry | a black ripe berry
rushcord = a braided loop | the bit of cord at my throat
drumskin = a tight dry skin | a skin stretched on a hoop
haulcry = a rough lifting call | the cry to set down
slap = the slap off two flat boards | the clack on the planks
shelter = the lee of a wall | a dry corner
stepsong = my counting tune | a walking air
marketbeat = a bustle of heels | a clatter of change
lastturn = the final turn | a little closing dip
heelmark = a dark heel mark | a scuffed half circle

any
opinion festivals for 2 : A wolf who can't afford the supper can still afford one turn with the music.
opinion church for 2 : Even a half-spoken blessing can reach the Bright One past the last scrap of breath.
opinion dole for 3 : Hunger sets such a fast time a wolf can't keep step with it. Food steadies the feet.
opinion drink against 1 : An evening cup's too dear when it takes tomorrow's balance as part of the price.
opinion houses against 2 : I worry about which House will let the line go slack just to spite the one holding the other end.
opinion sump for 1 : I can stamp my heels down here without a whole stairful asking what's broken.

grown
line greet : Step into the tune wherever it suits. | Plenty of space beyond my swinging elbow.
line greet [pair.band=strangers] : New feet keeping time beside mine. You're welcome. | A welcome from the head of this little procession.
line greet.return : I send your welcome round a second time. | A friendly word always sets me right on my feet.
line again.open : Round to the start of the figure already. | There's your step on the boards again.
line farewell : Travel to the easy beat while it lasts. | May your heels find somewhere dry at the finish.
line farewell.return : Your own way be clear underfoot. | I'll take that good wish away in my stride.
line react.news : Come close to tell it. I want the quiet parts too. | Carry on through the end of the measure.
line react.news.new : A turn I hadn't heard was coming. | First vibration of that to reach my end.
line react.news.known : I remember which way that one swung before. | My ear's already learned that measure.
line react.news.doubt : A step's missing in the middle of that telling. | I'll wait till two accounts can keep time together.
line react.news.glad [topic.kind=birth|marriage|work] : Good reason for a little dancing space tonight. | I could put my heels to that bit of news.
line react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=loss|death|assault] : I'd give the hurting wolves a little quiet round that news. | May the Bright One give the grieving some ease.
line ask.how : How's your breath holding on today's climb? | Found an easy pace for the work yet?
line answer.how : Still catching every beat I mean to catch. | There's breath enough left over for company.
line sympathise : Rest on this side. I can carry the conversation. | Nobody expects you to dance with a weight like that.
line ack : Yes. My ear's keeping time. | I've caught the shape of your meaning.
line refuse : My feet are wanted on a different errand first. | I'd leave you a promise I couldn't keep.
line accept_decline : Quite fair. A partner has to choose freely. | We'll catch another tune between us sometime.
line preclose : My feet have the next errand half begun already. | There's another call I've promised to answer.
line accept_preclose : Go on while the walking still costs little. | We can take the next turn when it comes.

scene quiet
when topic=pastimes self.likes=dancing
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I miss one step in every other figure. | There's a quiet step with no footfall at all.
b : Does it throw your partner? | A hop?
a : It's the same step each time. Soon there's two of us enjoying the hush. | More like changing your mind with one heel still up.


scene berries
when topic=food self.likes=blackberries
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I reach for the blackberry where the branch sags lowest. | I tap a ripe berry into my palm.
b : Is that one the sweetest? | Too soft for picking?
a : It's the least likely to stain my nose when the branch flies back. | The best ones make up their own minds to let go.


scene cord
when topic=faith self.piety=devout
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I close my paw round a cord to say a short blessing. | My prayer before a turn is for sound feet all round.
b : Does the Bright One need the reminder? | Even the feet that step on yours?
a : It's my wandering attention that needs catching. | Especially those. Mine are particularly interested.


scene planks
when topic=work self.job=sailor
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The planks under a cargo make a quite different music loaded and bare. | A job ashore still sways like a boat when six wolves take the weight.
b : Can you hear how heavy it is? | Do all six call the pace?
a : I can hear where to give another carrier room. | One call. The rest of the music comes from feet.


scene market
when topic=prices self.likes=market_bustle
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I like a market busy enough for the voices to run together. | At a busy market even the coin has a tune.
b : Can you pick out one particular seller then? | A tune you can dance to?
a : The berry seller takes tiny breaths between cries. I'm listening for the gap. | Only till my little handful's spent.


scene weather
when topic=weather self.dislikes=drizzle here.weather=rain
does tell.complaint / react.self / assess
a : Drizzle puts a catch just where the long note goes. | The little spit of rain gets inside my counting tune.
b : Was that a cough I heard? | Would shelter improve the music?
a : A change of note. By all means carry on talking. | It couldn't hurt. I'll call the move part of the dance.


scene wind
when topic=season self.likes=autumn_wind
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Autumn wind takes two steps for every one of mine. | I practise turning with the first rough wind of autumn.
b : Does it lead? | Is the wind a steady partner?
a : The leaves always seem to think so. | Disgraceful. I come out a better dancer for it.


scene haggle
when topic=prices self.dislikes=haggling
does tell.complaint / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A price that dances about ought to wear bells. | Haggling puts a stumble in the whole market queue.
b : So you can catch it cheap? | What if the seller expects it?
a : I'd hear it jingling and shop elsewhere. | I'd sooner spend my breath saying what good berries those are.


scene church
when topic=faith self.piety=devout
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : I like the little quiet after a blessing. | I ask for steadiness from the Bright One just as the cargo starts moving.
b : Are you waiting to hear something? | And if it still slips?
a : Somebody usually draws an easier breath. That's quite enough. | I put my whole shoulder to the work of keeping it up.


scene friend
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I could keep a good place for #self.friend# beside the music. | I'd like a friend to tell me if my step gets heavy.
b : How good a place? | Wouldn't that hurt your pride?
a : Within earshot of the gentler beats, far enough back to talk. | My pride can limp. My ankles need sound advice.


scene winter
when topic=dreams
does tell.feeling / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'm afraid the Houses might turn their shoulders against one another before winter. | I hope the Houses can pull on one line come winter.
b : A thing you've seen? | Are you expecting a quarrel?
a : A thing I'm dreading. Cold's hard enough without crossed arms. | I worry about one. Worry has never once been a full cargo of proof.


scene rope
when topic=work self.job=sailor
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My working step changes where a rope crosses the pier. | Two calls can sound much alike over the water.
b : Taller steps? | Which call do you move on?
a : More deliberate ones. There's no applause for a fine tumble into cargo. | The one from the crew I'm lifting with. I watch the shoulders too.


scene dusk
when topic=day here.time=dusk|night
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Dusk rubs the rough marks off the pier boards. | You can hear the day's last feet go by quite separately.
b : Safer to stop walking? | Where do the hurried steps go?
a : Safer to shorten the stride till I know the plank. | Same as mine. They come home and forget all about hurrying.


scene lean
when topic=times world.times=hard|lean
does tell.feeling / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Hard times steal a little breath from the end of every tune. | Thin purses make a thin sound at market.
b : Is there a short tune you keep? | Is the bustle any comfort?
a : Two steps and a turn. Enough for a pair to feel like company. | Yes. We can still give each other a fair amount of noise.


scene home
when topic=home self.street
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I could tell a tune from #self.street# by the echo. | Going home puts a lift into the left heel first.
b : Does the road sing differently? | Why the left?
a : In one narrow bit the end of every line comes hurrying back. | It's the first to turn off the main road.


scene faithless
when topic=health
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Sometimes I leave a little gap in my talking. | I trust my feet to give my breath a little rest.
b : To let somebody get a word in? | Won't walking cost you more breath?
a : Sometimes. Sometimes lungs want to speak for themselves. | With my voice at rest and my pace easy, I come out ahead.


scene gossip
when topic=gossip here.gossip=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I heard the words #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. | I heard more voices than I heard witnesses to that piece.
b : What tune do you set to that? | Does another voice add weight?
a : None. If I don't know the truth I won't help it dance. | Only when it's carrying a sight of its own.


scene green
when topic=pastimes self.likes=dancing
does invite / react.self / assess
a : Stand level with me and tap the ground three times. | No need to follow my feet exactly.
b : Do I turn now? | Won't that make two dances?
a : Take the quiet beat first. Now there's room to turn. | Two ways of coming round to the same place. I like seeing both.


story tub [topic=pastimes self.likes=dancing]
  : I once learned half a tune through a wall and practised it for a fortnight. It had a grand slapping finish.
  : When the door stood open I saw a wash tub and a board. No instrument anywhere.
  b : Did you give the tune up?
  : I finished the other half myself. Damp linen was a fair composer while it lasted.


story berryhem [topic=food self.likes=blackberries]
  : I picked blackberries into an apron with one corner lower than the other. A purple trail followed every homeward step.
  : A pup watching the trail said I'd invented a dance a wolf could learn after I'd gone.
  b : Did you have any berries left for supper?
  : One handful in the high corner. I ate them slowly and took a different route next time.


story echo [topic=faith self.piety=devout]
  : Alone in a bare room, I offered the Bright One a softly spoken prayer. The echo picked up only the last little bit.
  : I tried speaking more softly, until the words came back like breath through a reed.
  b : Could you still hear your prayer?
  : I'd stopped listening for my own voice by then. The quiet was the part I'd gone in search of.


rule @load
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=sailor
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Feet clear of the returning sling. | Hold that beat till all the weight is down.


rule @berry
when concept=bark self.likes=blackberries
does aside
cooldown 8h
say A hedge full of black fruit sets my feet moving. | Save the soft ones for the nearest mouth.


rule @drip
when concept=bark here.weather=rain
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Drizzle, your entrance missed the beat again. | My throat's perfectly capable of clearing itself.


rule @late
when concept=bark here.time=dusk
does aside
cooldown 8h
say The boards have an evening ring to them now. | Last light gets one figure all to itself.

dlg resident.hub : I've a good ear for company and a free one just now.
dlg resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, our feet have found the same patch again.
dlg resident.hub [here.time=night] : Even late feet tell what sort of day they've had.
dlg resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : Stand where you're comfortable. We can speak across a little distance.
dlg resident.job [self.job=sailor] : I put my shoulder under cargo and my feet where the crew needs them.
dlg resident.job : I'll take anything that lets a wolf work beside a good steady pair of paws.
dlg resident.news [world.news] : The news carried this far. #world.news#.
dlg resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : These were the words. #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. I can't vouch for the tune.
dlg resident.bye : Walk with a steady tread and the Bright One's blessing.

graft resident.hub
choice Show me that step you left out? -> count_four
node count_four
say Count four, but touch the floor only on one, two and four. The empty beat lets your partner get an elbow round.
free
choice What if nobody takes the gap? -> count_four_more
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node count_four_more
say I leave it there anyway. A dancer's entitled to some say about the next move.
choice I'll give your heels some room. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye
